Trained checkpoints live here.

They are ~2.4 GB in total and are therefore NOT in the git repository. The
checkpoint archive link will be added with the public release; see the "Model
checkpoints" section of README.md. Unpack the archive into this directory so that
e.g.

    models/capsule_mnist_best_dynamic.pt
    models/ablation_predictor.pt

exist. `./reproduce.sh --artifacts` checks for the first of these and stops with
instructions if it is missing.

`make recompute` re-derives the paper's central statistics from the committed
per-observation records in results/ and diffs them against the committed values.
It needs no GPU and no dataset; only its final parameter-count check reads the
checkpoints in this directory.
